In what sense are gismu fundamental?  They are not semantic primes.  That t=
hey can be used to express or define every concept (never actually claimed)=
 depends more upon their number than anything else.  They are on many lists=
 of most common concepts or ones likely to be found in every language.  The=
y are pretty clearly not concepts that cannot be otherwise expressed.  This=
 not to say we don't need a gismu for rotation or, at least, a redefinition=
 of some other word in the area.

Sent from my iPad

